---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const internal = (segment) => `${base}/${segment.replace(/^\//, '')}`;
---
<Layout
  title="Definition"
  description="Canonical definition v0.3: Agalmic Research as an open practice for converting available abundance into durable capability by identifying and relaxing real constraints."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Canonical programme definition · v0.3</p>
      <h1>What Agalmic Research is for now.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Agalmic Research is an open practice of disciplined inquiry and building that asks how available abundance can be converted into durable capability by identifying and relaxing real constraints.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell thesis">
      <p class="eyebrow">Canonical definition</p>
      <blockquote>Agalmic Research is an open practice of disciplined inquiry and building that asks how available abundance can be converted into durable capability by identifying and relaxing real constraints.</blockquote>
      <p>It begins inwardly with real work and the capabilities of the practitioner. It asks what is actually limiting useful action, what knowledge, tools, computation, institutions or other resources are already abundant enough to help, and whether using them produces a durable increase in understanding, judgment, skill or practical capacity.</p>
      <p>It prefers inheritance to reinvention. Existing scholarship, standards, curricula, open-source software and prior art are treated as infrastructure to understand and reuse. Novelty is welcome when contribution requires discovery, but novelty is not the programme's primary currency.</p>
      <p>When the practice produces something genuinely reusable, a tool, protocol, implementation, curriculum, dataset, research result, negative result or clearer route through existing knowledge, outward contribution is encouraged. It is an exit path from useful work, not an obligation to make every exploration public.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What changed</p>
        <h2>Research moved from destination to method.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">Earlier versions emphasized expanding worthwhile futures and establishing a broad research programme around abundance and shifting scarcity.</p>
        <p>Adversarial boundary work showed that many of the underlying mechanisms already have mature antecedents in economics, innovation studies, learning science, HCI and other fields. The current response is not to search anxiously for a narrower novelty claim. It is to use that inherited knowledge.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Research remains essential for lineage, testing, criticism, provenance and correction. It no longer has to be the primary output.</strong></p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Inward before outward</p>
        <h2>Use the practitioner as the first testbed.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The immediate programme asks whether abundant machine cognition and existing human knowledge can expand capability in areas that already matter: scholarliness, software engineering, engineering leadership and Nemosyne.</p>
        <p>Success is not defined by producing more artefacts. Where capability formation is the objective, success requires evidence that the person can later understand, reconstruct, judge, create or defend more with less scaffolding.</p>
        <p><a href={internal('practice')}>See the current practice →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Scholarliness & authority</p>
        <h2>Capability can grow. Authority still requires warrant.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Training may increase subject mastery, conceptual precision, methodological judgment, calibration and the ability to defend claims. That expansion is valuable.</p>
        <p>But no capability tracker, AI tutor or self-directed programme can confer epistemic authority by itself. Authority remains claim-sensitive and answerable to evidence, methods, relevant expertise, criticism and appropriate handoff.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Expand the capacity from which authority can be earned; never substitute training history for warrant.</strong></p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell thesis">
      <p class="eyebrow">Compact form</p>
      <blockquote>Use abundance to expand capability. Begin with the constraint in front of you.</blockquote>
      <p>A second operating maxim remains useful: <strong>seek contribution before novelty; seek novelty only where contribution requires discovery.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
